      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Consider a linear transformation $T:{R}^{7}\\to {R}^{7}.$ If $\\text{rank}(T)=3$ then $\\text{nullity}(T)=$",
      "worked_solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $T:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given transformation, we have $n=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(T) & =7 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(T) & =7-3 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
